---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Conceptual Homes | Hairness"
	description="Possible specialized Hairness Homes, clearly separated from what Hairness 0.5 alpha ships today."
	path="/homes/"
>
	<SiteHeader />
	<main>
		<header class="learn-hero shell">
			<p class="eyebrow">Conceptual · Not installable yet</p>
			<h1>What could a specialized Home be built for?</h1>
			<p>
				These are product directions, not catalog entries. Hairness 0.5 provides
				the framework; it does not ship these specialized Homes.
			</p>
		</header>

		<article class="learn-content shell">
			<section>
				<p class="section-index">01 · Composition</p>
				<h2>A coherent Home organizes more than invocation.</h2>
				<div class="anatomy-grid">
					<article><span>01</span><h3>Inhabitants</h3><p>Who collaborates here?</p></article>
					<article><span>02</span><h3>Conventions</h3><p>How is judgment exercised?</p></article>
					<article><span>03</span><h3>Continuity</h3><p>What deserves to survive sessions?</p></article>
					<article><span>04</span><h3>Assets</h3><p>What equips the work?</p></article>
					<article><span>05</span><h3>Artifacts</h3><p>What results are worth governing?</p></article>
					<article><span>06</span><h3>Targets</h3><p>Where does work land without being absorbed?</p></article>
					<article><span>07</span><h3>Agent Runtimes</h3><p>What remains when the runtime changes?</p></article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<p class="section-index">02 · More than the low level</p>
				<h2>Skills are useful. They are not the organizing idea.</h2>
				<div class="definition-stack">
					<div><strong>Skill</strong><span>A model-facing entrypoint to a capability.</span></div>
					<div><strong>Asset</strong><span>A reusable product for work: instructions, tools, knowledge, workflows or runtime.</span></div>
					<div><strong>Home</strong><span>A coherent environment that owns and composes Assets for people, agents and Targets.</span></div>
					<div><strong>Hairness</strong><span>The framework that makes the environment portable, inspectable and source-owned.</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<p class="section-index">03 · Product truth</p>
				<h2>Ideas, directions and available products are different promises.</h2>
				<div class="maturity-grid">
					<article>
						<p class="concept-status">Imagined usage</p>
						<h3>Make the paradigm visible</h3>
						<p>A thought experiment reveals what becomes possible without claiming an implementation.</p>
					</article>
					<article>
						<p class="concept-status">Conceptual Home</p>
						<h3>Describe a coherent composition</h3>
						<p>The inhabitants, Assets, Artifacts and Targets fit together, but the Home is not installable.</p>
					</article>
					<article class="maturity-live">
						<p class="concept-status">Installable Home</p>
						<h3>Deliver the composition</h3>
						<p>Sources, contracts and runtime exist and can be inspected before use.</p>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<p class="section-index">04 · Three thought experiments</p>
				<h2>Start with the work, then design its Home.</h2>
				<div class="home-experiments">
					<article>
						<header><p>Concept · Not installable yet</p><h3>Game Development Home</h3></header>
						<ul>
							<li>Engine and studio conventions as shared Assets</li>
							<li>Playtest reports and design decisions as Artifacts</li>
							<li>Games, tools and documentation as independent Targets</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
					<article>
						<header><p>Concept · Not installable yet</p><h3>Designer Home</h3></header>
						<ul>
							<li>Research and critique methods that survive clients</li>
							<li>Design-system knowledge without trapping it in one app</li>
							<li>Deliverables that keep evidence and lineage</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
					<article>
						<header><p>Concept · Not installable yet</p><h3>Research Home</h3></header>
						<ul>
							<li>Evidence standards and reading practices as Assets</li>
							<li>Claims, syntheses and decisions as governed Artifacts</li>
							<li>Projects and publications as separate Targets</li>
						</ul>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="home-question">
				<p class="eyebrow">Conceptual direction</p>
				<h2>If your agents had a Home, what would yours be built for?</h2>
				<p>
					What would you preserve across sessions? What would you equip every
					agent with? And what would you finally remove from your repositories?
				</p>
				<div class="hero-actions">
					<a class="button button-primary" href="/#create-home">Install Hairness</a>
					<a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/thevzion/hairness">Inspect the framework ↗</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</article>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
